{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head 2c4297abbea11f6d7f7b59871513b8504d015270. I reviewed the merge alone, as you asked, and c1c7df14 stands for the rest. Only documents and notes differ from main b0af01d2 (`git diff --name-only` shows no other path), so no gate is owed.\n\n**The 250 lines and the 25.** I recounted independently from merge base ada88648: 250 lines added on main, and 25 not verbatim here by a whitespace-normalized match. I read the counterpart of each 25, and each carries main's fact:\n- `cli.md`: the `dap install` synopsis lines, the `separate-recovery` table row and its paragraph, and the policy `keys` read at `:509`.\n- `deploy.md`: the rollout section at `:166-181`, `SESSION_SECRET` at `:46-47` with `trust-boundaries.md:70`, and the 900 seconds at `:230`.\n- `mcp.md:2009`, `scopes.md:789`, and `trust-boundaries.md` steps 1, 2, 4 and 5 and the two run paragraphs at `:153-155`.\n\nThe other direction holds too. Of the 22 document lines of 25 characters or more that main removed, none survives here. \"Nothing was sent\", \"stays readable for at most\" and \"Revoking by ID has run once\" appear in neither tree, and the count of \"founder key\" matches main.\n\n**The relocated section and the links.** The new deploy section sits under \"Roll out new creation versions\", and its heading gives `cli.md` a working link. check-doc-links passes with 997 links and 0 broken, including main's links that now point at `#dap-act`, `#dap-items` and `#settings-the-order-uses`.\n\n**The four changes beyond main's text: all fine.**\n- The synopsis's `commons` matches the table, and `--host none` already names that cohort.\n- The links follow the rewritten headings.\n- \"Operator\" for \"planner\" in the run paragraphs is right for a public page. An operator did run those calls, and the evidence stays in the notes.\n- Dropping the legacy selector from `cli.md`'s `keys` sentence loses nothing, because the rest of that sentence and `deploy.md#the-order` still